  "body": "The spec says:\n\n> This specification defines a [policy-controlled feature](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-permissions-policy/#policy-controlled-feature), identified by the token \"usb\", that controls whether the [usb](https://usb.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-navigator-usb) attribute is exposed on the [Navigator](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#navigator) object.\n\nHowever, the implemented behavior in Chromium is to define navigator.usb and check if the site is allowed to use \"usb\" (with [ShouldBlockUsbServiceCall](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webusb/usb.cc;l=127;drc=689c4fe9f23645596a2c5cfba414cad67fd5d7c9)) when calling [getDevices](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webusb/usb.cc;l=203;drc=e697e53d5dac9bf42b29351d0127cf9245704347) or [requestDevice](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webusb/usb.cc;l=230;drc=e697e53d5dac9bf42b29351d0127cf9245704347).\n\n\n\n",
